SUMMARY:Build an Agent Day - Atlanta
DESCRIPTION:All Things AI (Live)\nJoin us in [Atlanta for Build an Agent D
 ay](https://www.buildanagent.io/events/atlanta-ga) and craft your own AI a
 gent live and in person! One day. One working AI agent\, built by you.\n\n
 ## [Build an Agent Day - Atlanta](https://www.buildanagent.io/events/atlan
 ta-ga)\n\n**Walk in with a workflow you hate. Walk out with an agent that 
 does it for you.**\n\nBuild An Agent Day is a one-day\, hands-on workshop 
 where you codify a real task from your job as a working AI agent — and l
 eave with the design pattern to do it again and again. No slide decks to t
 ake home. By 6 PM you have something running against your own Google Works
 pace or Microsoft 365 account.\nIt's a program of [All Things AI](https://
 allthingsai.org/ "https://allthingsai.org") and [All Things Open](https://
 allthingsopen.org/ "https://allthingsopen.org")\, built for the people who
  do the work: business professionals\, government leaders\, and K-12 and h
 igher-ed educators. If you can write a clear how-to email\, you can build 
 an agent here.\n\n#### What you'll build\n\nOver eight hours\, you'll buil
 d the same workflow across three agent stacks and pick the one that fits y
 our environment:\n\n* **Claude Cowork** (Anthropic) — for knowledge work
 ers\n* **ChatGPT Agents** (OpenAI) — for enterprise IT\n* **Manus** — 
 for research-heavy roles\n\nThe arc: pick a workflow you own (reports\, in
 take\, scheduling\, drafting\, research)\, capture your expertise as a ski
 ll an AI can follow\, wire it into your stack\, and ship it the same day. 
 You'll demo it before you leave.\n\n#### A sample of the day\n\n* **Crack 
 Open the Agent** — the three primitives (model\, tools\, memory) and the
  agent loop\, narrated tool call by tool call\n* **Pick Your First Three A
 gents** — Mark's S.M.A.R.T. framework to sort your tasks by AI readiness
  and match each to AI\, Human\, or Both\n* **Write Your First Skill** — 
 the anatomy of a SKILL.md\, plus worked examples including an "anti-slop" 
 quality skill and a composed website-audit skill\n* **Ship an Autonomous R
 esearch Agent** — build a Morning Brief in Manus that triages email\, pr
 eps your calendar\, and ranks the day's industry news\n* **Working lunch\,
  three stacks\, three tables** — poke at all three with food in front of
  you\n\nThe full eight-hour arc runs at every city stop. Because every wor
 kshop is live\, the schedule flexes to the room.\n\n#### Who's teaching\n\
 n**Mark Hinkle** — Workshop instructor. Founder of The AIE Network (250\
 ,000+ subscribers)\, co-founder of All Things AI\, 30+ years in emerging t
 ech across cloud.com\, the Linux Foundation\, and the Node.js Foundation. 
 An operator\, not a consultant.\n**Todd Lewis** — Co-founder\, All Thing
 s Open. More than a decade running technology events in the Carolinas (POS
 CON\, Open Source 101\, All Things Open).\n\n#### What's included\n\n* Eig
 ht hours of hands-on building\n* All three agent stacks\n* Meals and mater
 ials\n* The working agent you walk out with\n* A year of community access 
 across All Things Open\, All Things AI\, and The AIE Network — meetups\,
  virtual events\, and ongoing learning\n\n#### Pricing\n\n* **Early bird: 
 $297** (first 100 registrants)\n* **Standard: $397**\n\nAll tiers are all-
 inclusive. Most employers reimburse the ticket under professional developm
 ent or continuing education budgets — receipts formatted for expense rep
 orts available on request.
